This isn't patching, this is already into the compiling stage.
patching is what you do with the patch -program.


Anyway, you have either MENU_COLOR_REGEX or MENU_COLOR_REGEX_POSIX
defined in config.h, just comment them out.


MENU_COLOR_REGEX will make menucolors use a regex library of the
GNU variant, and MENU_COLOR_REGEX_POSIX will use a POSIXy one.

(Unfortunately there is no regex library on windows[1], so you can't use
them.)

If neither of those is defined, then menucolors will use globbing,
that is, the basic ? and * wildcards.



[1] There are some ports of at least the GNU regex lib, but I haven't
managed to make any work.

